# Netlify redirect rules (copied into the build, so they apply whatever the site's base folder is).
# Rules are checked from top to bottom.

# 1. Forward API calls to the Render backend. The browser only talks to the Netlify site,
#    so the login cookie stays first-party (Safari and others block cross-site cookies).
#    Change the address if your Render service URL is different.
/api/*    https://shopsphere-api-b4te.onrender.com/api/:splat    200!

# 2. Single-page app: every other path loads index.html and React Router shows the page.
/*        /index.html    200
